# 4. CREATIVE CONCEPT: "BEEP TO RECEIPT"

One barcode scan at a till touches hardware, operating system, network, application, cloud/automation and people/process. The site follows that single transaction down through those layers. The journey ends at a printed receipt, which is my experience and contact section.

Entry: a short premise line, for example "One scan. Six layers. Here is what happens between the beep and the receipt." No loading screen and no intro that delays content.

Six strata, each with: a title, a one-line description of what happens to the scan at this layer, a distinct visualization, 2-4 annotations linking to Atlas nodes, and evidence badges.
1. Hardware and peripherals - scanner, terminal, receipt printer, cabling. Visual: SVG schematic line drawing.
2. Operating system and device - drivers, processes, filesystem. Visual: process tree or file tree.
3. Network - LAN, router, WAN, Layers 1-4. Visual: node graph hosting the packet routing simulation.
4. Application - POS software, SaaS administration, data. Visual: structured record and log view.
5. Cloud and automation - SaaS, cloud foundations, scripting, RPA, integrations. Visual: flow diagram. Show only what the content supports, with honest statuses.
6. People and process - vendor coordination, support, deployments, handoffs. Visual: handoff or ticket-lifecycle diagram.
Security, AI-assisted development and similar topics are cross-cutting themes shown as nodes (and later as highlight lenses), not as strata.

Signature element: one continuous SVG trace line running through the strata and changing representation at each one. Its position encodes scroll progress. Under reduced motion or without scroll-driven support it is fully drawn and static.

Views: Trace (default), Atlas, Plain. A compact persistent header shows the name, the view switch, and "Experience" and "Contact" links that jump to the Receipt. A recruiter must reach experience and contact within one interaction, without needing any animation to complete.

